<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Treatable psychological conditions (#17 redesign). Unlike vanilla illnesses these do NOT resolve
    on their own — no immunity, no natural severity decline. They persist until therapy drives severity
    to zero (SynapseTherapyConditions.Treat), and while untreated the pawn falls into the linked mental
    state more often, scaled by severity (SynapseTherapyConditions.TickChaos). Severity 0..1; the stages
    are display bands. Not medically tendable — therapy in the patient's own bedroom is the treatment.
  -->

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Trauma</defName>
    <label>trauma</label>
    <description>A deep, unresolved traumatic wound. Left untreated it intrudes without warning — the mind is dragged back into the moment. Talking it through, patiently and in private, is the only thing that lastingly helps.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.72, 0.5, 0.82)</defaultLabelColor>
    <stages>
      <li><label>mild</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>moderate</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>severe</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Depression</defName>
    <label>depression</label>
    <description>A persistent, heavy low that colours everything. It does not lift by itself; without help the person withdraws and gives up more and more. Steady, private counselling slowly loosens its grip.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.45, 0.55, 0.72)</defaultLabelColor>
    <stages>
      <li><label>mild</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>moderate</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>severe</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Anxiety</defName>
    <label>anxiety disorder</label>
    <description>A chronic, jangling dread. Untreated it boils over into panic at the worst moments. Being talked down and reassured, again and again in a safe place, is what eventually settles it.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.85, 0.72, 0.42)</defaultLabelColor>
    <stages>
      <li><label>mild</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>moderate</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>severe</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Bipolar</defName>
    <label>bipolar disorder</label>
    <description>Violent swings between crushing lows and reckless, euphoric highs. Left untreated the highs turn dangerous. Steady counselling — and, ideally, mood stabilisers — evens the peaks and troughs out.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.62, 0.42, 0.72)</defaultLabelColor>
    <stages>
      <li><label>mild</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>moderate</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>severe</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Neurotic</defName>
    <label>neurosis</label>
    <description>A raw, over-reactive temperament that frays at the smallest setback and breaks far more often than most. Patient, repeated counselling gradually thickens their skin.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.80, 0.66, 0.50)</defaultLabelColor>
    <stages>
      <li><label>mild</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>moderate</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>severe</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    Pyromania is CHRONIC (like a genetic drug dependency): it never truly goes away. Therapy MANAGES it —
    holding severity low so the urge rarely takes over — but the seeding trait is never lifted, and without
    ongoing treatment the compulsion creeps back and they go and set fires. Modelled with curable=false and a
    managed floor in SynapseTherapyConditions.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Pyromania</defName>
    <label>pyromania</label>
    <description>An irresistible fascination with fire. It cannot be cured, only kept in check — steady therapy holds the compulsion down so it rarely surfaces, but neglect it and the urge to set things alight comes roaring back.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.88, 0.45, 0.28)</defaultLabelColor>
    <stages>
      <li><label>managed</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>restless</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>compulsive</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    Grief is the first EVENT-driven condition: it arises when someone close dies, not from a trait, and unlike
    the others it slowly fades on its own (the SeverityPerDay comp). Therapy accelerates that fade; left alone
    a severe grief still eases over a couple of weeks. Not seeded or worsened by SynapseTherapyConditions
    (no trait), so its only progression is the comp's natural decline.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>Synapse_Hediff_Grief</defName>
    <label>grief</label>
    <description>The raw ache of a loss that hasn't been processed. It dulls with time, but sitting with someone who will listen speeds the healing and keeps it from curdling into something worse.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.55, 0.58, 0.62)</defaultLabelColor>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-0.08</severityPerDay>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li><label>numb</label><minSeverity>0</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>mourning</label><minSeverity>0.4</minSeverity></li>
      <li><label>inconsolable</label><minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity></li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
